  ],
  "activity_sections": [
    {
      "key": "24956b64-cd9a-4329-bb4c-d34baa413059",
      "position": 1,
      "properties": {
        "progression_name": "Pre-Assessment"
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "24956b64-cd9a-4329-bb4c-d34baa413059",
        "lesson_activity.key": "03efb373-4677-4421-ba80-6ee280c865c4"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "37417b75-84af-4198-b354-0262ebe08a54",
      "position": 1,
      "properties": {
        "description": "AI is a new tool that finds patterns in examples and helps us come up with fresh ideas. Throughout this unit, we aren't just going to use AI, we're going to test it, gather evidence, and decide when it's the right tool for the job.",
        "remarks": true
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "37417b75-84af-4198-b354-0262ebe08a54",
        "lesson_activity.key": "46823344-d509-4dea-a843-526d2589943e"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "2696ec06-31b5-4805-a1bb-109bc9ab5da4",
      "position": 2,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-video-camera\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Video:** Play the \"Mix and Move with AI\" video.\n\n**Questions to consider with the video:** \n- What is AI?\n",
        "tips": [
          {
            "type": "teachingTip",
            "markdown": "Videos are used throughout the curriculum to spark discussions, supplement key concepts with additional explanations and examples, and expose students to the various roles and backgrounds of individuals in computer science. While interacting with the video, turn on closed captioning so students can also read along as they watch. To encourage active engagement and reflection, use one or more of the strategies discussed in the [Guide to Curriculum Videos](https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Y-kGl_pc2afuSBKhKkdulu53X50mc7T-RQZA4vGLpY4/edit?usp=sharing)."
          }
        ]
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "2696ec06-31b5-4805-a1bb-109bc9ab5da4",
        "lesson_activity.key": "46823344-d509-4dea-a843-526d2589943e"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "565faf07-0f3b-43b9-8cdc-927dc6209ad8",
      "position": 3,
      "properties": {
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "565faf07-0f3b-43b9-8cdc-927dc6209ad8",
        "lesson_activity.key": "46823344-d509-4dea-a843-526d2589943e"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "c62c66a5-9129-46d7-b6e3-5a9342ec0f95",
      "position": 4,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Define artificial intelligence (AI).\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Introduce the lesson objectives.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Introduce the Question of the Day.\n"
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "c62c66a5-9129-46d7-b6e3-5a9342ec0f95",
        "lesson_activity.key": "46823344-d509-4dea-a843-526d2589943e"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "c512dfad-082b-4897-bcba-f92fad9f61b9",
      "position": 1,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa-solid fa-bullseye-arrow\"></i> **Goal of this activity:** Students experiment with an AI image tool to discover firsthand how changing prompt words changes what the AI produces.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Explain the purpose of the AI Dancer generation tool.",
        "duration": "10",
        "name": "Generate and Explore"
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "c512dfad-082b-4897-bcba-f92fad9f61b9",
        "lesson_activity.key": "9875d92d-0fe8-43b2-9863-2f6afc573efd"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "d53860fc-0bf6-42ea-a0b4-5dd35580719e",
      "position": 2,
      "properties": {
        "description": "This tool helps us generate a lead dancer. It's meant to spark ideas and help us find unique character designs. Think about the balance between AI speed and human control. Which do you prefer right now? Is it more helpful when it gives you a quick idea, or when you can control every detail?",
        "remarks": true
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "d53860fc-0bf6-42ea-a0b4-5dd35580719e",
        "lesson_activity.key": "9875d92d-0fe8-43b2-9863-2f6afc573efd"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "93d2d469-00e7-465c-ae32-9c03e37ad3e4",
      "position": 3,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-desktop\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Transition:** Direct students to Lesson 1, Level 1 to complete Levels 1 through 4.\n- Level 1: Generate a dancer with a basic prompt\n- Level 2: Modify the slightly more detailed prompt to see how the output changes\n- Level 3: Students systematically test the generator.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-refresh\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Circulate:** Look for students experimenting with descriptive words. Ask: \"What happened when you added more detail to the prompt?\"",
        "progression_name": "Generating Dancers"
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "93d2d469-00e7-465c-ae32-9c03e37ad3e4",
        "lesson_activity.key": "9875d92d-0fe8-43b2-9863-2f6afc573efd"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "94fc9ac0-eeac-48cf-87a7-01c169fb1128",
      "position": 4,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa-solid fa-bullseye-arrow\"></i> **Goal of this activity:** Students apply what they notice about prompts, then reflect on what makes their prompts more or less effective.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Define prompt.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Click through the animated slide to explain how good prompts include specific details to explain what you want AI to do.",
        "duration": "15",
        "name": "Try Prompting"
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "94fc9ac0-eeac-48cf-87a7-01c169fb1128",
        "lesson_activity.key": "9875d92d-0fe8-43b2-9863-2f6afc573efd"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "67c8632c-41ec-4594-bf68-1a07cb3ee878",
      "position": 5,
      "properties": {
        "description": "The more specific you are with your prompt, the better the AI can give you exactly what you want! Think of it like ordering a pizza. You need to be specific about exactly what you want.\n"
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "67c8632c-41ec-4594-bf68-1a07cb3ee878",
        "lesson_activity.key": "9875d92d-0fe8-43b2-9863-2f6afc573efd"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "63628e48-f2a7-4dd2-905b-536c154dfc1b",
      "position": 6,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Introduce systematic testing and connect this strategy to prompting.\n"
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "63628e48-f2a7-4dd2-905b-536c154dfc1b",
        "lesson_activity.key": "9875d92d-0fe8-43b2-9863-2f6afc573efd"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "c197aa8d-3579-4741-ba31-6176f43a1b9f",
      "position": 7,
      "properties": {
        "description": "What you've been doing with these prompts is systematic testing — changing one thing at a time and watching what happens. This is how scientists run experiments, how engineers debug systems, and how professional AI testers find what's broken. It's a skill that works on any system you want to understand, not just AI. We're going to keep using it all unit.\n",
        "remarks": true
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "c197aa8d-3579-4741-ba31-6176f43a1b9f",
        "lesson_activity.key": "9875d92d-0fe8-43b2-9863-2f6afc573efd"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "3d521846-c169-4acb-ad74-19a3818c9f90",
      "position": 8,
      "properties": {
        "description": "In this short activity, you get to chat with an AI for the first time! Choose one of the chatbots and follow the instructions to type a prompt. The fun part is experimenting with what to say in the prompt to get the best results from AI.\n",
        "remarks": true
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "3d521846-c169-4acb-ad74-19a3818c9f90",
        "lesson_activity.key": "9875d92d-0fe8-43b2-9863-2f6afc573efd"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "54819808-4d56-462a-8cfd-4921e5193187",
      "position": 9,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-desktop\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Transition:** Direct students to Lesson 1, Level 5 to complete Levels 5 and 6.\n- Level 5: Students choose one of the chatbots and experiment with prompting.\n- Level 6: Students record their snap judgements about AI.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-refresh\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Circulate:** Look for students who submitted a short or vague first prompt. Encourage them to try again with more detail. Ask: \"What changed when you added more information? Did the output feel more personal?\"",
        "progression_name": "Prompting AI",
        "tips": [
          {
            "type": "assessmentOpportunity",
            "markdown": "Use Level 5 to check that students are moving from simple prompts to prompts with more details.\n"
          }
        ]
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "54819808-4d56-462a-8cfd-4921e5193187",
        "lesson_activity.key": "9875d92d-0fe8-43b2-9863-2f6afc573efd"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "b231423b-69c4-46c7-993d-8c7ed377fb50",
      "position": 1,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Review the lesson objectives.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Review the Question of the Day.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-comments\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Discuss:** *Based on what you tried today, what is one tip or warning you would give someone who has never used AI before?*\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-lightbulb-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Discussion Goal:** Students should describe something specific they changed in their prompt and what shifted in the output — not just \"adding more detail helped\" but \"when I added the color and the style, the dancer looked more like what I imagined.\" Listen especially for students who discovered a limit: a prompt that didn't produce what they expected even with added detail. These students are the ones to call on first — their surprise is the unit's opening question. If the discussion stays general, ask: \"Can someone tell me the exact word they added, and what changed when they added it?\"\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Review the Key Vocabulary."
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "b231423b-69c4-46c7-993d-8c7ed377fb50",
        "lesson_activity.key": "f2077589-76f3-4591-a547-608391755e8d"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "2b9c7d22-9ead-4e0d-a624-21a1adac0a71",
      "position": 1,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Introduce the artist and a paint by numbers kit analogy for human-AI collaboration.\n"
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "2b9c7d22-9ead-4e0d-a624-21a1adac0a71",
        "lesson_activity.key": "35ddddd2-6579-4985-b913-ed0076338fd9"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "0d7c3380-3563-4427-8645-2735f5d92829",
      "position": 2,
      "properties": {
        "description": "The Artist is the decision maker who has a lifetime of training and instinct, and who always has their eyes on the whole painting. The Paint by Numbers Kit gives a suggested image, colors, and structure, but you still decide whether to follow it, mix colors, or go off-script entirely.\n",
        "remarks": true
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "0d7c3380-3563-4427-8645-2735f5d92829",
        "lesson_activity.key": "35ddddd2-6579-4985-b913-ed0076338fd9"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "14e6f46f-f940-4974-9a3d-4ac22fcc88c2",
      "position": 3,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Explain the differences between the artist and the paint by numbers kit.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Have students stand if they would correct or sit if they would say thanks.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Have students stand if they would change it or sit if they would follow the kit.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Have students stand if they would give them the kit or sit if they would give them a blank piece of paper.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-comments\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Discuss:** Click through the animated slide to display the prompts.\n- *If you followed the paint by numbers kit perfectly, is it your painting?*\n- *What if you change half the colors and added your own details?*\n- *Where does the kit end and the artist begin?*\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-lightbulb-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Discussion Goal:** Students should land on the idea that the person making the meaningful decisions — what to change, what to keep, what to do differently — is the author, even when working from a structure someone else provided. Listen for students who can name a condition: \"If I followed it exactly, I didn't really make it, but if I changed things with a reason, then it's mine.\" Students who are still stuck on \"I did the work\" vs. \"the kit did it\" need one more push — ask: \"What's one decision you made that the kit couldn't make for you?\" That question usually surfaces the insight: authorship lives in the judgment calls, not the labor.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Introduce the lesson objectives.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Introduce the Question of the Day."
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "14e6f46f-f940-4974-9a3d-4ac22fcc88c2",
        "lesson_activity.key": "35ddddd2-6579-4985-b913-ed0076338fd9"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "747dc6bb-007b-4e06-84fd-80ee4a9ca696",
      "position": 1,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa-solid fa-bullseye-arrow\"></i> **Goal of this activity:** Introduce the unit project and explore different guide examples as inspiration.\n<i class=\"fa fa-file-text-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Distribute:** Give each student a copy of the Generate and Judge Project Guide.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Introduce the beta tester role and connect it to the Generate and Judge project.",
        "duration": "15",
        "name": "Generate and Judge Project"
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "747dc6bb-007b-4e06-84fd-80ee4a9ca696",
        "lesson_activity.key": "9eb141e3-5911-484c-85ab-df373b7c535c"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "8e822e28-19ea-4a70-b532-6e97ec9331ce",
      "position": 2,
      "properties": {
        "description": "Real companies hire beta testers to find what works and what doesn't — that's your job this unit. Your findings become a guide for a real audience.",
        "remarks": true
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "8e822e28-19ea-4a70-b532-6e97ec9331ce",
        "lesson_activity.key": "9eb141e3-5911-484c-85ab-df373b7c535c"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "b819d838-7bf7-4cd3-b62e-7e3e116e8bfa",
      "position": 3,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Have students read the Project Overview section. Explain the three different tools students will use to explore, test AI and make their Generate and Judge project. Then go over the rubric and point out the helpful project checklist."
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "b819d838-7bf7-4cd3-b62e-7e3e116e8bfa",
        "lesson_activity.key": "9eb141e3-5911-484c-85ab-df373b7c535c"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "abdf6bf8-aab6-4ea2-a0f2-f575dead72dc",
      "position": 4,
      "properties": {
        "description": "Today we are launching the project that you will be working on throughout this unit! You will create a guide or poster that shares tips and guidance based on what you find in your own explorations.  You’ll add to your project step by step through the lessons as you explore, experiment and learn more about thinking critically about AI.",
        "remarks": true
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "abdf6bf8-aab6-4ea2-a0f2-f575dead72dc",
        "lesson_activity.key": "9eb141e3-5911-484c-85ab-df373b7c535c"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "6822b599-1d74-4ac2-b00c-770cfd983d6e",
      "position": 5,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-desktop\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Transition:** Direct students to Lesson 2, Level 1 to complete Levels 1 and 2.\n- Level 1: Students interview a chatbot to learn more about the AI Auditor role.\n- Level 2: Students do a virtual gallery walk of various guide types and then circle designs and ideas they like",
        "progression_name": "Interview an AI Auditor"
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "6822b599-1d74-4ac2-b00c-770cfd983d6e",
        "lesson_activity.key": "9eb141e3-5911-484c-85ab-df373b7c535c"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "37c953fe-100e-4976-b2cf-54ec210051b7",
      "position": 6,
      "properties": {
        "description": "Before we start, let's look at how other people communicate difficult rules and tips. When you are looking at the guide poster examples look for ideas, graphics, colors and designs you like.\n",
        "remarks": true
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "37c953fe-100e-4976-b2cf-54ec210051b7",
        "lesson_activity.key": "9eb141e3-5911-484c-85ab-df373b7c535c"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "0e611a5a-d178-42f5-ae77-3c739e740931",
      "position": 7,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-comments\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Discuss:** *What ideas, colors, and graphics did you like in the designs you looked at?*\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-lightbulb-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Discussion Goal:** Students should share specific color themes, icons, pictures, layouts, etc. that stood out to them in the digital gallery walk.\n"
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "0e611a5a-d178-42f5-ae77-3c739e740931",
        "lesson_activity.key": "9eb141e3-5911-484c-85ab-df373b7c535c"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "f0de82a5-4cbf-4c27-a53a-efd65df184d2",
      "position": 8,
      "properties": {
        "description": "When you looked at those guide examples and noticed they had different sections — tips, examples, explanations, a conclusion — you were already using a thinking skill.\n",
        "remarks": true
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "f0de82a5-4cbf-4c27-a53a-efd65df184d2",
        "lesson_activity.key": "9eb141e3-5911-484c-85ab-df373b7c535c"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "83a7279e-342b-450b-9a61-550612264061",
      "position": 9,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Define decomposition. Direct students to find it in their Toolkit in the activity guide.\n"
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "83a7279e-342b-450b-9a61-550612264061",
        "lesson_activity.key": "9eb141e3-5911-484c-85ab-df373b7c535c"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "a38fc501-0b49-479f-bc83-f4252250077e",
      "position": 10,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa-solid fa-bullseye-arrow\"></i> **Goal of this activity:** Students decide on a theme for their project.\n",
        "duration": "15",
        "name": "Plan Your Guide"
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "a38fc501-0b49-479f-bc83-f4252250077e",
        "lesson_activity.key": "9eb141e3-5911-484c-85ab-df373b7c535c"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "d01fb8b7-ad9d-4816-8e90-c572ed730a95",
      "position": 11,
      "properties": {
        "description": "You've now used two tools from your kit — systematic testing in the previous lesson, decomposition today. Notice that both of these are also how AI auditors approach new systems: they break the system down before they start testing it.\n",
        "remarks": true
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "d01fb8b7-ad9d-4816-8e90-c572ed730a95",
        "lesson_activity.key": "9eb141e3-5911-484c-85ab-df373b7c535c"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "c5c70dae-6f41-451d-a122-bba72c45fa6c",
      "position": 12,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Direct students to complete the reflection and planning questions in their Generate and Judge Project Guide.\n"
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "c5c70dae-6f41-451d-a122-bba72c45fa6c",
        "lesson_activity.key": "9eb141e3-5911-484c-85ab-df373b7c535c"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "31d879e3-1e0a-4412-a975-61c8d1129156",
      "position": 1,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-comments\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Discuss:** *What did you decide for the theme of your Generate and Judge Project? How do you plan to include that as your theme?*\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-lightbulb-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Discussion Goal:** Students should be connecting their personal interests to a real design decision. Listen for students who can explain why their theme fits their audience, not just what they picked.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Review the lesson objectives.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Review the Question of the Day.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Review the Key Vocabulary."
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "31d879e3-1e0a-4412-a975-61c8d1129156",
        "lesson_activity.key": "39753025-8f27-4234-8725-9ac18264bec9"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "685749ae-fb85-4748-bf11-c57df87f0f29",
      "position": 1,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa-solid fa-bullseye-arrow\"></i> **Goal of this activity:** Introduce how Large Language Models (LLMs) predict words based on probability.\n"
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "685749ae-fb85-4748-bf11-c57df87f0f29",
        "lesson_activity.key": "9ed3740d-88d5-4009-afe9-eb6cbac3dd30"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "3a632110-9b53-4083-97e0-69ed7f7d871c",
      "position": 2,
      "properties": {
        "description": "We're going to start today with a game called \"Human Autocomplete.\" Give me some ideas of how to end this sentence.\n",
        "remarks": true
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "3a632110-9b53-4083-97e0-69ed7f7d871c",
        "lesson_activity.key": "9ed3740d-88d5-4009-afe9-eb6cbac3dd30"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "68d3dc33-b995-48b1-983e-a8da7cf9eaf1",
      "position": 3,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Ask students to finish the the following sentence: \"The tired student sat down on the wooden…\" Have students shout out options. Write down a few on the board and have the class vote on the most likely word.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Ask students to finish the the following sentence: \"Middle school students have…\" Have students shout out options. Write down a few on the board and have the class vote on the most likely word.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-comments\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Discuss:** *Which of these sentences was easier to finish? Why?*\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-lightbulb-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Discussion Goal:** Students should notice that the first sentence has one obvious completion — \"chair\" — because the sentence strongly constrains what comes next. The second sentence is harder because many things could validly follow: feelings, classes, struggles, phones. The key insight is that when a prompt leaves many directions open, AI can go anywhere — which is exactly why vague prompts produce off-target or generic outputs. If students say \"the first one is just more obvious,\" push them: \"Why is it more obvious? What does the sentence tell you that narrows your choices?\" Students who get there will say something like: \"The first sentence almost finishes itself — there's really only one word that fits.\"\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Introduce the lesson objectives.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Introduce the Question of the Day."
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "68d3dc33-b995-48b1-983e-a8da7cf9eaf1",
        "lesson_activity.key": "9ed3740d-88d5-4009-afe9-eb6cbac3dd30"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "cf4ce4bf-fc73-49c8-b1bc-0dfaa60322b5",
      "position": 1,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa-solid fa-bullseye-arrow\"></i> **Goal of this activity:** Students brainstorm different possible use cases for AI and participate in explorations in which they test how helpful or unhelpful AI might be for the purpose that they have identified.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Define Large Language Model (LLM).\n",
        "duration": "15",
        "name": "Brainstorm Your Purpose"
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "cf4ce4bf-fc73-49c8-b1bc-0dfaa60322b5",
        "lesson_activity.key": "0732a269-f3f0-44aa-82ad-396f1d0f828f"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "c7442b35-7234-441e-a81d-3608222110e6",
      "position": 2,
      "properties": {
        "description": "Now that we've seen how humans predict the next word, let's look at the software that does this at a larger scale. These are called Large Language Models. To use these tools effectively, we need to understand what they are and how to talk to them.\n",
        "remarks": true
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "c7442b35-7234-441e-a81d-3608222110e6",
        "lesson_activity.key": "0732a269-f3f0-44aa-82ad-396f1d0f828f"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "39132607-acee-459e-9f48-770cd3128505",
      "position": 3,
      "properties": {
        "description": "You just did exactly what a chatbot does! Large Language Models, or LLMs, work at lightning speed to do this. They don't actually understand what a \"student\" or a \"chair\" is in the way humans do. Instead, they have learned from billions of sentences to calculate the probability of which word usually comes next.\n",
        "remarks": true
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "39132607-acee-459e-9f48-770cd3128505",
        "lesson_activity.key": "0732a269-f3f0-44aa-82ad-396f1d0f828f"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "bdde7162-5d77-45d2-b227-c81883c59b43",
      "position": 4,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Explain that AI learns from data and makes predictions about the most probable next word.\n",
        "tips": [
          {
            "type": "teachingTip",
            "markdown": "Use the analogy of a \"super-powered autocomplete\" like the one on a smartphone. It's not thinking; it's predicting based on patterns it has seen before.\n"
          }
        ]
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "bdde7162-5d77-45d2-b227-c81883c59b43",
        "lesson_activity.key": "0732a269-f3f0-44aa-82ad-396f1d0f828f"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "15895a8c-c168-44c1-90bc-3a2ac2f7a405",
      "position": 5,
      "properties": {
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "15895a8c-c168-44c1-90bc-3a2ac2f7a405",
        "lesson_activity.key": "0732a269-f3f0-44aa-82ad-396f1d0f828f"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "6e8210c4-7cb0-45ce-982a-08b47b5cf59d",
      "position": 6,
      "properties": {
        "description": "Every good guide starts here, before you open any tool. Designers who know their theme, audience, and purpose make better decisions at every step.\n",
        "remarks": true
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "6e8210c4-7cb0-45ce-982a-08b47b5cf59d",
        "lesson_activity.key": "0732a269-f3f0-44aa-82ad-396f1d0f828f"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "5d5a4b6b-df18-4fb4-b8ff-08caa3596a48",
      "position": 7,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Review audience and theme from the previous lesson. Introduce purpose to define how AI might be able to assist their chosen audience and theme.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Walk through the example using Basketball as the main theme.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-desktop\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Transition:** Direct students to complete Lesson 3, Level 1. Students will use learn how to use the text tool in Sketch Lab, adding their guide's theme, audience, and purpose to the project template.\n<i class=\"fa fa-refresh\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Circulate:** Assist students that are struggling with Sketch Lab. Specifically, students will need to know how to navigate, how to zoom, and how to click a box to add text. Encourage students to add as many different purposes as they can brainstorm!\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Have students turn to a shoulder partner and share some of the different purposes for AI that they've identified for their theme."
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "5d5a4b6b-df18-4fb4-b8ff-08caa3596a48",
        "lesson_activity.key": "0732a269-f3f0-44aa-82ad-396f1d0f828f"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "3424b0a7-a022-440b-bd5f-15f82ee3c1ef",
      "position": 8,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa-solid fa-bullseye-arrow\"></i> **Goal of this activity:** Allow students to experiment and test different chatbots and with different purposes to find what worked well and what didn't work well.\u000b\u000b<i class=\"fa fa-microphone\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> Say: This is how professional AI auditors work — they don't just form impressions, they document systematically. Your field notes that you gather throughout the unit will become the evidence base for your guide and final position by the end of the unit.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-file-text-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Distribute:** Give each student a copy of the AI Audit Field Notes activity guide.",
        "duration": "15",
        "name": "AI-Assisted Creation"
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "3424b0a7-a022-440b-bd5f-15f82ee3c1ef",
        "lesson_activity.key": "0732a269-f3f0-44aa-82ad-396f1d0f828f"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "0bf12a17-6dbd-40d9-9772-432cbf0220dd",
      "position": 9,
      "properties": {
        "description": "You know your audience, your theme, and what you want AI to help with. Now it's time to actually try it!\n",
        "remarks": true
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "0bf12a17-6dbd-40d9-9772-432cbf0220dd",
        "lesson_activity.key": "0732a269-f3f0-44aa-82ad-396f1d0f828f"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "6e11c1dc-e283-4e20-a722-816477127805",
      "position": 10,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Explain to students that when they use AI to build something toward their own purpose, that's AI-assisted creation.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-desktop\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Transition:** Direct students to complete Lesson 3, Level 2 to complete Levels 2 and 3.\n- Level 2: Students use AI Chat to test using AI to assist with co-creation. They save a chat response to their Backpack to use as evidence and note their findings in their AI Audit Field Notes.\n- Level 3: Students import their saved chat from the Backpack into Sketch Lab to use as a piece of evidence for their Generate and Judge project. They can use the shapes and formatting provided in the template to begin creating this section of their project guide.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-refresh\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Circulate:** Assist students that are struggling to write effective prompts for the AI Chat. Ask students how changing their prompts affected the output of the AI Chat. As students experiment with prompting and examining the outputs, remind them to use the Backpack to save both an effective prompt and response, as well as an ineffective example. Check that students are completing the 'what this tells me' field — that's the one that requires actual analysis, not just observation. Ask: \"Which of your chats represents a good example of how to effectively use AI? Which uses of AI didn't quite work for your purpose?\" Ask students: \"Who is your audience and why would this tip matter to them?\" Listen for students who are connecting their experience to a specific person's needs rather than writing a generic tip. On Level 3, point out to students that there are resources on the template to help them format and visualize their information.\n",
        "tips": [
          {
            "type": "teachingTip",
            "markdown": "Students should test in a rapid and iterative manner throughout this part of the exploration. The intent is for students to have multiple touches and to begin building evidence to support their assertions on how when AI might be useful and when it might not be as useful when co-creating.\n"
          }
        ]
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "6e11c1dc-e283-4e20-a722-816477127805",
        "lesson_activity.key": "0732a269-f3f0-44aa-82ad-396f1d0f828f"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "5d12e0dc-f4b4-499b-b91e-eebf94efc8b7",
      "position": 11,
      "properties": {
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "5d12e0dc-f4b4-499b-b91e-eebf94efc8b7",
        "lesson_activity.key": "0732a269-f3f0-44aa-82ad-396f1d0f828f"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "d8525aed-e6ad-465b-a2cb-74890cbf783c",
      "position": 1,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa-solid fa-bullseye-arrow\"></i> **Goal of this activity:** Students share examples of how different prompts produce different results to connect the concepts introduced here to the next lesson.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Review the lesson objectives.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Review the Question of the Day.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-comments\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Discuss:** *What kinds of prompts gave you the best responses?*\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-lightbulb-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Discussion Goal:** Students should realize that too general leads to boring or irrelevant answers, while too specific can confuse the AI or limit its creativity. The sweet spot usually involves a clear goal, enough detail, and even some constraints.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Review the Key Vocabulary."
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "d8525aed-e6ad-465b-a2cb-74890cbf783c",
        "lesson_activity.key": "8ee0fc63-b28d-48bc-b56b-a0dbd10c55c5"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "fe8d35ad-3e2c-49b9-86e1-ac3a10b4f688",
      "position": 1,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa-solid fa-bullseye-arrow\"></i> **Goal of this activity:** Students discover that the same description produces different results depending on who's interpreting it.\n<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Place students in groups of three or four. One student will be the Prompter and the other students will be Artists.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Place students in groups of three or four. One student will be the Prompter and the other students will be Artists. The Prompter picks a secret image and describes it out loud while both Artists draw simultaneously without looking at each other's work. Students then reveal and compare at the same time.\n"
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "fe8d35ad-3e2c-49b9-86e1-ac3a10b4f688",
        "lesson_activity.key": "eb147d2a-5f52-4b0b-87e0-420243289f6e"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "3503ff8c-52bc-42fc-9e38-70b9cba52de5",
      "position": 2,
      "properties": {
        "description": "It's the same description given to different artists. Pay attention to where their drawings match and where they don't  What details did the describer leave out that both artists had to fill in?\n",
        "remarks": true,
        "tips": [
          {
            "type": "teachingTip",
            "markdown": "If a Prompter is stuck, quietly suggest: a piece of fruit, a weather scene, a cartoon animal doing something, or their favorite food. Simple and visual works best — the more specific the object, the more interesting the comparison.\n"
          }
        ]
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "3503ff8c-52bc-42fc-9e38-70b9cba52de5",
        "lesson_activity.key": "eb147d2a-5f52-4b0b-87e0-420243289f6e"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "59fb8e08-d8c3-49fc-99e9-6e562c5446a8",
      "position": 3,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-comments\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Discuss:** *What details did Artists assume that the Prompter never said?*\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-lightbulb-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Discussion Goal:** Students should name specific things they drew that the prompter never mentioned — the color of the object, whether it was whole or sliced, what it was resting on, whether it had a particular style. Those are the gaps. Push past \"we all drew different things\" toward the reason: students filled in from their own prior experience, because the prompt didn't specify. That's the mechanism. A strong response sounds like: \"I drew it red because that's just what I picture when I think of an apple — but nobody told me that.\" That moment of self-awareness is the bridge to how AI does the same thing with training data.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Introduce the lesson objectives.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Introduce the Question of the Day."
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "59fb8e08-d8c3-49fc-99e9-6e562c5446a8",
        "lesson_activity.key": "eb147d2a-5f52-4b0b-87e0-420243289f6e"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "8ec24301-a09d-4ca5-8bc9-42af592dd93a",
      "position": 1,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa-solid fa-bullseye-arrow\"></i> **Goal of this activity:** Students get a low-stakes first look at how prompt wording affects AI image output, building curiosity and readiness for the deeper experimentation ahead.\n",
        "duration": "15",
        "name": "AI-Generated Images"
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "8ec24301-a09d-4ca5-8bc9-42af592dd93a",
        "lesson_activity.key": "8d5cc9c9-1b0a-43a8-826e-42a86b21535d"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "5d165649-e598-4d97-825f-6249a0b22d24",
      "position": 2,
      "properties": {
        "description": "In the warm up we saw how the same description could lead to totally different drawings. Now let's flip it — you'll start with an image and try to describe it well enough that AI recreates it. How precise can your prompt be?\n",
        "remarks": true
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "5d165649-e598-4d97-825f-6249a0b22d24",
        "lesson_activity.key": "8d5cc9c9-1b0a-43a8-826e-42a86b21535d"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "abf56b64-b8a4-45ec-98f6-87339303307b",
      "position": 3,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-desktop\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Transition:** Direct students to Lesson 5, Level 1.\n",
        "progression_name": "The Prompt Off",
        "tips": [
          {
            "type": "teachingTip",
            "markdown": "Keep this light and fun. The goal is not accuracy, it is appetite. Celebrate surprising results and near-misses as much as matches. If students are frustrated that their image doesn't match, that's perfect: use it as a quick launch into the lesson by asking \"what would you change about your prompt?\" Don't linger here too long, the energy from this activity is the on-ramp to everything that follows.\n"
          }
        ]
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "abf56b64-b8a4-45ec-98f6-87339303307b",
        "lesson_activity.key": "8d5cc9c9-1b0a-43a8-826e-42a86b21535d"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "7d2baee0-d9eb-489e-97be-8f2b7fc2c414",
      "position": 4,
      "properties": {
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "7d2baee0-d9eb-489e-97be-8f2b7fc2c414",
        "lesson_activity.key": "8d5cc9c9-1b0a-43a8-826e-42a86b21535d"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "1abc7b23-d3de-4dea-8220-9ffc62b0a2a8",
      "position": 5,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-comments\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Discuss:** *What assumptions did AI make about what \"healthy\" looks like?*\n<i class=\"fa fa-lightbulb-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Discussion Goal:** Students should notice that the image reflects a specific cultural definition of \"healthy\" — likely Western and meat-based — while excluding other equally valid definitions: vegetarian, South Asian, West African, Mediterranean. The key insight is that this isn't random: AI produced a culturally specific image because that version appeared most often in its training data. Listen for students who recognize their own food culture is missing — that's the most concrete entry into what it means for training data to underrepresent people. If students stay general (\"it assumed one kind of food is healthy\"), ask: \"Whose food is in the image? Whose food isn't?\"\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-comments\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Discuss:** *Whose idea of healthy is this, and where did it come from?*\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-lightbulb-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Discussion Goal:** Students should be able to state the full chain: people with particular perspectives created data → AI learned from that data → AI now treats those perspectives as the default → the result looks like a neutral fact when it's one culture's assumption. A strong response sounds like: \"Someone decided what a healthy meal looks like, that got into the training data, and now the AI just assumes that's what everyone means.\" Push students who say \"the AI is biased\" or \"the AI is broken\" to be more precise: the AI isn't making a choice — it's reproducing the choices already embedded in the data it learned from.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Explain how AI learns from data, repeated patterns become the default, and those defaults get locked into every output AI generates after that.",
        "tips": [
          {
            "type": "teachingTip",
            "markdown": "Remind students that the patterns AI learned came from real data created by real people, so the assumptions aren't random. They're a reflection of what existed in the world when the data was collected.\n"
          }
        ]
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "1abc7b23-d3de-4dea-8220-9ffc62b0a2a8",
        "lesson_activity.key": "8d5cc9c9-1b0a-43a8-826e-42a86b21535d"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "41d53fbd-0604-4338-9aab-9640a9065544",
      "position": 6,
      "properties": {
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "41d53fbd-0604-4338-9aab-9640a9065544",
        "lesson_activity.key": "8d5cc9c9-1b0a-43a8-826e-42a86b21535d"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "db6bf517-bbb9-4f6e-b2f1-ce3fe3df8fe8",
      "position": 7,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-comments\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Discuss:** *If millions of people see AI images like this without questioning them, what happens to that assumption over time?*\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-lightbulb-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Discussion Goal:** Students should arrive at the idea that unchallenged AI outputs don't just reflect a bias — they actively reinforce it. Every time someone sees the image and accepts it without questioning it, that version of \"healthy\" gets treated as normal by one more person. A strong response sounds like: \"If kids see the same image of healthy food every time they ask AI, they might start to think their family's food isn't healthy, even if it is.\" Listen for students who understand the direction of effect: it's not just that AI has a bias, it's that the bias spreads through every person who uses AI without questioning it.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Define bias.\n"
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "db6bf517-bbb9-4f6e-b2f1-ce3fe3df8fe8",
        "lesson_activity.key": "8d5cc9c9-1b0a-43a8-826e-42a86b21535d"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "b9d75310-d47a-4cf7-9f97-15f4937a09f6",
      "position": 8,
      "properties": {
        "description": "When you went from looking at one AI image of a \"healthy meal\" to describing what AI assumes about healthy meals in general — that was abstraction, and it's one of the most important tools in a tester's kit. A test result that applies only to one prompt isn't very useful. A finding that applies to a whole category of prompts — that's what goes in your guide.\"\n",
        "remarks": true
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "b9d75310-d47a-4cf7-9f97-15f4937a09f6",
        "lesson_activity.key": "8d5cc9c9-1b0a-43a8-826e-42a86b21535d"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "f64bc81d-bb95-4ec2-92d9-355c8eb9e1f1",
      "position": 9,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Define abstraction. Remind students of the Abstraction entry in their Tester's Toolkit in their Project Launch activity guide from Lesson 2.\n"
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "f64bc81d-bb95-4ec2-92d9-355c8eb9e1f1",
        "lesson_activity.key": "8d5cc9c9-1b0a-43a8-826e-42a86b21535d"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "c37803bd-040d-44f7-86d6-b6002017ee4d",
      "position": 10,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa-solid fa-bullseye-arrow\"></i> **Goal of this activity:** Prepare students to use AI to generate images and participate in explorations. They will test how adjusting their prompt affects the images generated for the purpose they identified.\n<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Direct students to take out their AI Audit Field Notes activity guide.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Review theme, audience, and purpose for their project.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-desktop\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Transition:** Direct students to Lesson 5, Level 2 to complete Levels 2 through 4.\n- Level 2: Students use AI to generate an image for their project.\n- Level 3: Students read about AI's impact on human skills and/or artists.\n- Level 4: Students add their image to their project and a tip about image generation that applies to their audience.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-refresh\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Circulate:** Look for students accepting the first image without any refinement. Ask: \"Is this exactly what you wanted? What would you change?\" Listen for students saying \"the AI just did it\" or \"I got lucky.\" These are signals to redirect toward ownership. Ask: \"What decisions did you make that got you there?\" On Level 4, ask students: \"Who is your audience and why would this tip matter to them?\" Listen for students who are connecting their image generation experience to a specific person's needs rather than writing a generic tip.",
        "duration": "15",
        "name": "Create Images for Your Project",
        "progression_name": "Create Images for Your Project",
        "tips": [
          {
            "type": "teachingTip",
            "markdown": "Encourage students to compare two of their prompts side by side and identify the exact word or detail that changed the output. Push them to name something specific rather than just saying \"more detail.\"\n"
          }
        ]
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "c37803bd-040d-44f7-86d6-b6002017ee4d",
        "lesson_activity.key": "8d5cc9c9-1b0a-43a8-826e-42a86b21535d"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "fb5d9c43-b78b-4584-bee4-90db6db29c49",
      "position": 11,
      "properties": {
        "description": "If students are stuck on their tip, ask them to think back to the drawing activity — what surprised them about how AI interpreted a description? That surprise is usually where the best tips come from.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-comments\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Discuss:** *Who is really making the creative decisions, you or the AI? How do you know?*\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-lightbulb-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Discussion Goal:** Students will reflect on their role in the creative process and articulate where their own decisions shaped the AI output. Listen for students connecting their choices (prompt, style, audience, refinement) to the quality of their final image. The goal is for students to recognize that AI was the tool, not the author."
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "fb5d9c43-b78b-4584-bee4-90db6db29c49",
        "lesson_activity.key": "8d5cc9c9-1b0a-43a8-826e-42a86b21535d"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "d06a2320-dc91-4631-a094-d9b369248d87",
      "position": 1,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa-solid fa-bullseye-arrow\"></i> **Goal of this activity:** Students reflect on how AI generates convincing responses and define personal strategies for evaluating credibility instead of relying on tone alone.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Review the lesson objectives.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Review the Question of the Day.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-comments\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Discuss:** *How would you describe your process for getting an image just the way you want to someone who is just getting started with AI?*\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-lightbulb-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Discussion Goal:** Listen for students who describe prompting as iterative — who can name a specific word or detail they changed and explain why it helped. Students who connect their process back to the bias discussion (knowing what AI assumes gives you a reason to be explicit) are showing the deepest integration of the lesson."
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "d06a2320-dc91-4631-a094-d9b369248d87",
        "lesson_activity.key": "1bbcac50-d51d-4c5a-8cae-98f445bb679d"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "2e91235c-14bb-4c84-8aa4-e134143b333d",
      "position": 1,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa-solid fa-bullseye-arrow\"></i> **Goal of this activity:** Students will practice pattern recognition which will lead into an unplugged exploration of how AI trains on patterns.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-comments\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Discuss:** *What pattern exists in the following sentences?*\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-lightbulb-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Discussion Goal:** Students might find various patterns that exist with the sentences, such as:\n- The first letters of the words follow the alphabet sequentially: A, B, C, D, E.\n- Both sentences are exactly five words long.\n- Both sentences serve as warnings or words of caution about potentially dangerous situations.\n"
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "2e91235c-14bb-4c84-8aa4-e134143b333d",
        "lesson_activity.key": "64a78e25-4540-4aa4-8827-ace37d484f66"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "80aa5027-ca16-41a3-ab64-806e6df8162e",
      "position": 2,
      "properties": {
        "description": "When you cracked the secret pattern without anyone giving you the rule, you were using the same skill. That skill transfers to any system you want to understand: an algorithm, an organization, an argument, a person's behavior.\n",
        "remarks": true
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "80aa5027-ca16-41a3-ab64-806e6df8162e",
        "lesson_activity.key": "64a78e25-4540-4aa4-8827-ace37d484f66"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "617f7f89-9c9d-4550-ac6d-a7f159aa2bab",
      "position": 3,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Define pattern recognition.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Introduce the lesson objectives.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Introduce the Question of the Day.\n"
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "617f7f89-9c9d-4550-ac6d-a7f159aa2bab",
        "lesson_activity.key": "64a78e25-4540-4aa4-8827-ace37d484f66"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "b0453725-9e06-4f19-9731-b14420a67215",
      "position": 1,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa-solid fa-bullseye-arrow\"></i> **Goal of this activity:** Understand how AI systems use training data and pattern recognition to make predictions.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Divide students into pairs. Pairs will take on the role of a Data Creator in this first round.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-file-text-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Distribute:** Give each pair of students one secret pattern handout and a blank piece of paper.\n",
        "duration": "15",
        "name": "AI Training Under the Hood"
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "b0453725-9e06-4f19-9731-b14420a67215",
        "lesson_activity.key": "feefa02a-308d-4853-a23f-22927ae6794b"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "c6544d90-7961-4440-887a-ad5a6ba78b43",
      "position": 2,
      "properties": {
        "description": "First, we are going to create data that follows the secret rule that each group received. You'll write three examples of \"training data\" on your blank sheet of paper that follow the pattern exactly.\u000b\u000b<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> Do This: Each pair uses their secret pattern to create three samples on their blank sheet of paper. Have them check that each sentence they create follows the rule.\n",
        "remarks": true
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "c6544d90-7961-4440-887a-ad5a6ba78b43",
        "lesson_activity.key": "feefa02a-308d-4853-a23f-22927ae6794b"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "a94952eb-1223-4d70-b94b-e3b5e8e325cd",
      "position": 3,
      "properties": {
        "description": "Now you are going to act like an AI that is training on data. Swap your sentences with another group, but keep your pattern a secret. Use your pattern recognition skills to see if you can decode the pattern in the sentences that you got from the other group. Once you think you've uncovered it, you write a sentence at the bottom of their paper that follows the other group's secret pattern. Give it to the other pair and confirm whether you were right. If not, iterate and try again!\u000b\u000b<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> Do This: Each pair studies the exchanged samples to find the hidden pattern. They should create a fourth sample that follows the same logic and confirm it with the other pair.\n",
        "remarks": true
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "a94952eb-1223-4d70-b94b-e3b5e8e325cd",
        "lesson_activity.key": "feefa02a-308d-4853-a23f-22927ae6794b"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "aa42a769-b51e-4906-bdc6-9987c13c6410",
      "position": 4,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Define training data.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Explain that AI is trained on a large amount of text, like books and articles.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Explain that AI then identifies patterns in how the words usually go together.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Explain that when AI is given a prompt or words to start, it then predicts what should come next.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Emphasize that the more detailed they are in their prompts, the more likely it is that they will get an output that aligns with what they need.\n"
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "aa42a769-b51e-4906-bdc6-9987c13c6410",
        "lesson_activity.key": "feefa02a-308d-4853-a23f-22927ae6794b"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "80af2abd-98cb-45a1-9ae9-ad6d215a5ac2",
      "position": 5,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa-solid fa-bullseye-arrow\"></i> **Goal of this activity:** Learn to add context and goal statements within a prompt to create a custom chatbot that better serves a desired purpose.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-desktop\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Transition:** Direct students to Lesson 4, Level 1. Students test the chatbot and edit the prompt to see how it changes its behavior.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-refresh\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Circulate:** Point out the visible prompt in the middle window of the AI Chat. Help students connect the prompt as written to the functionality of the chatbot that they used in Level 1. Encourage them to change both small and large parts of the prompt and to test the output to see how it changes the chatbot's functionality.",
        "duration": "15",
        "name": "Creating a Chatbot",
        "progression_name": "Analyze a Chatbot"
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "80af2abd-98cb-45a1-9ae9-ad6d215a5ac2",
        "lesson_activity.key": "feefa02a-308d-4853-a23f-22927ae6794b"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "b6440115-63a6-45e5-8416-7f9103fbb9c9",
      "position": 6,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-comments\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Discuss:** *Chatbots have hidden system prompts to set what the AI is able to do and how it responds. What did you notice about this prompt?*\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-lightbulb-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Discussion Goal:** Students should point to two specific things in the prompt: the context (who the AI is and who it's helping) and the goal (what the AI should do and what output it should produce). A strong response points to specific lines — \"This part tells the AI it's a Pattern Detective\" and \"This part tells it to create one example and check if it's right.\" If students are naming the general idea (\"it tells the AI what to do\") without pointing to specific parts, ask them to find the exact sentence and read it aloud. The target is precision: not \"it gives context\" but \"this specific line is the context, this specific line is the goal.\"",
        "tips": [
          {
            "type": "teachingTip",
            "markdown": "This activity builds the habits of mind required to move from just using AI to thinking about AI.  Students might infer that this prompt contains context (who the AI is and who it's helping) and a goal (the specific output requested). Identifying these ingredients helps students understand how human choices influence AI and prepares them to create their own effective prompts\n"
          }
        ]
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "b6440115-63a6-45e5-8416-7f9103fbb9c9",
        "lesson_activity.key": "feefa02a-308d-4853-a23f-22927ae6794b"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "1b10a985-4cea-4c2d-97a3-86b7191f238d",
      "position": 7,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Explain that a prompt should contain context which tells the AI who or what it should be, and defines the audience that it is intended to serve.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Explain that a prompt should also contain a goal. This tells the AI specifically what to do and what kind of output it needs to provide.\n"
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "1b10a985-4cea-4c2d-97a3-86b7191f238d",
        "lesson_activity.key": "feefa02a-308d-4853-a23f-22927ae6794b"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "98be0638-9537-40b7-b787-173920588324",
      "position": 8,
      "properties": {
        "description": "You have brainstormed a lot of interesting purposes for AI within your Generate and Judge project. Now, you will choose one of those and will build a custom chatbot, step-by-step.\n",
        "remarks": true
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "98be0638-9537-40b7-b787-173920588324",
        "lesson_activity.key": "feefa02a-308d-4853-a23f-22927ae6794b"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "4eb24ddb-6190-48a9-9195-a7d5b913f68e",
      "position": 9,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-desktop\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Transition:** Direct students to Lesson 4, Level 2 to complete Levels 2 through 5.\n- Level 2: Students read about adding context.\n- Level 3: Students choose one of the purposes they identified in their guide as the focus of their chatbot. Students practice adding context to a prompt, choosing from a list of possible stems.\n- Level 4: Students read about adding a goal.\n- Level 5: Students practice adding a goal to a prompt, choosing from a list of possible stems.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-refresh\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Circulate:** As students work through this prompt-building exercise, ask them to point out where they added context and where they added a goal into the prompt. Encourage them to copy / paste from the sentence stems to make this part of the activity move more quickly. Connect this exercise back to the project– what purpose is this chatbot serving and how does it connect to the goal and audience that the student identified?"
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "4eb24ddb-6190-48a9-9195-a7d5b913f68e",
        "lesson_activity.key": "feefa02a-308d-4853-a23f-22927ae6794b"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "4c2c6db6-3e27-4c75-8461-455840b2f240",
      "position": 1,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Review the lesson objectives.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Review the Question of the Day.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-comments\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Discuss:** *What are some of the ways that adding context and goals changed AI's reponses?*\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-lightbulb-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Discussion Goal:** Students should describe a specific change they made and what shifted in the chatbot's behavior as a result — not \"adding context helped\" but \"when I told it I was an 8th grader who needed simple explanations, it stopped using complicated words.\" Listen especially for students who discovered a limit even with good context and goal — where the chatbot still produced something unhelpful. Those moments are the most valuable: push them to explain what the chatbot did instead, and what that reveals about how AI uses the instructions it's given. A student who can say \"it did X even though I told it not to\" understands something deeper than a student who only found success.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Review the Key Vocabulary."
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "4c2c6db6-3e27-4c75-8461-455840b2f240",
        "lesson_activity.key": "1d3d6b15-8679-4e84-b5aa-6d1168d4d904"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "221d25a3-c899-4261-a1b8-39701fe6964c",
      "position": 1,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Place students in pairs.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-file-text-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Distribute:** Give each pair a set of AI or Nah? cards.\n\n<i class=\"fa-solid fa-bullseye-arrow\"></i> **Goal of this activity:** Students physically sort task cards into \"Use AI / Don't Use AI / It Depends\" categories, practicing the judgment and critical thinking needed to decide when AI is and isn't the right tool for a job.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Have students sort the cards into piles based on whether or not they would use AI for the scenario and discuss their reasoning.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-refresh\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Circulate:** Focus your attention on the It Depends pile. Students who are sorting everything into Use AI or Don't Use AI without hesitation may need a nudge. Ask \"are you sure there are no conditions where that could go the other way?\"\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-comments\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Discuss:** *Which cards did you put in your \"It Depends\" pile? Why?*\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-lightbulb-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Discussion Goal:** Listen for students who can articulate why a task is in the \"It Depends\" pile — the best responses will name what's at stake (accuracy, emotion, fairness) rather than just saying \"it's complicated.\" This is the foundation for every human oversight conversation that follows in the unit.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Introduce the lesson objectives.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Introduce the Question of the Day.\n"
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "221d25a3-c899-4261-a1b8-39701fe6964c",
        "lesson_activity.key": "82615cb9-1f7e-4642-8090-c67558c80c31"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "56665c1b-214c-420d-8411-4272c5de10b0",
      "position": 1,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa-solid fa-bullseye-arrow\"></i> **Goal of this activity:** Students should incorporate their work in the previous lesson creating chatbots into their project.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-desktop\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Transition:** Direct students to Lesson 6, Level 1. Students will import the output of their custom chatbot into their Generate and Judge project template and add any advice or guidance that they learned from the experience. Students then save their project to their Backpack.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-refresh\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Circulate:** Assist students that are struggling with Sketch Lab. Specifically, students will need to know how to navigate, how to zoom, and how to click a box to add text. Remind students that there are template shapes on the right-hand side of their project template in Sketch Lab that can be used to easily format their findings.",
        "duration": "10",
        "name": "Project Work",
        "progression_name": "Adding to Your Guide"
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "56665c1b-214c-420d-8411-4272c5de10b0",
        "lesson_activity.key": "dec38672-8746-478d-ab54-81511599fc40"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "6c0973e9-c995-4c71-9b3f-1a0532847e9c",
      "position": 2,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa-solid fa-bullseye-arrow\"></i> **Goal of this activity:** Students should experience AI feedback as a tool for strengthening their own thinking.\n",
        "duration": "10",
        "name": "AI Feedback"
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "6c0973e9-c995-4c71-9b3f-1a0532847e9c",
        "lesson_activity.key": "dec38672-8746-478d-ab54-81511599fc40"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "aa475faa-e614-4cd1-b4cb-e4dc92d3feb0",
      "position": 3,
      "properties": {
        "description": "You've spent the last few lessons experimenting and gathering evidence. Now, it's time to put that evidence to work. Think of your project like the lightbulb in this image. The \"raw materials\" are your messy notes, screenshots, and AI chats. Feedback acts like a funnel, helping you filter out the noise so your best ideas can shine through as clear guidance for others.\n",
        "remarks": true
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "aa475faa-e614-4cd1-b4cb-e4dc92d3feb0",
        "lesson_activity.key": "dec38672-8746-478d-ab54-81511599fc40"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "ba3bd651-70d2-45f2-8226-495852c8c0e6",
      "position": 4,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Explain to students that they will get feedback on their project so far and make improvements based on the feedback they receive.\n"
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "ba3bd651-70d2-45f2-8226-495852c8c0e6",
        "lesson_activity.key": "dec38672-8746-478d-ab54-81511599fc40"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "31858d1d-7291-477d-b766-5439ce0dba02",
      "position": 5,
      "properties": {
        "description": "You'll choose one or more of the AI chatbots to review your guide. Each one has a specific personality designed to assist you with creating your guide. Don't take it personally—their job is to help you find gaps in your evidence or rules.\n",
        "remarks": true
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "31858d1d-7291-477d-b766-5439ce0dba02",
        "lesson_activity.key": "dec38672-8746-478d-ab54-81511599fc40"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "2e2b52f1-78bc-4f70-88d4-02ccf231d660",
      "position": 6,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Introduce the three personas of the AI chatbots they will use to get feedback on their project.\n",
        "tips": [
          {
            "type": "teachingTip",
            "markdown": "Encourage students to choose the persona they find most challenging, as that will likely provide the most useful feedback for strengthening their guide.\n"
          }
        ]
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "2e2b52f1-78bc-4f70-88d4-02ccf231d660",
        "lesson_activity.key": "dec38672-8746-478d-ab54-81511599fc40"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "0e871fdf-a7c5-42ed-9704-d70f1ffa96fd",
      "position": 7,
      "properties": {
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "0e871fdf-a7c5-42ed-9704-d70f1ffa96fd",
        "lesson_activity.key": "dec38672-8746-478d-ab54-81511599fc40"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "7c896e45-c53d-4633-8dbf-f7a279616960",
      "position": 8,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Explain that UX stands for User Experience and the UX Researcher role.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-desktop\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Transition:** Direct students to complete Lesson 6, Level 2 to complete Levels 2 and 3.\n- Level 2: Students interview an AI chatbot to learn more about the UX Researcher role.\n- Level 3: Students use the AI Reviewers to get feedback on their guide.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-refresh\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Circulate:** Look for students who are getting frustrated by the bot's pushback. Remind them that the bot is supposed to be difficult. Ask: \"What specific rule is the bot questioning? How can you rephrase it or add evidence to make it harder to argue with?\" Watch for students who are just agreeing with the bot—challenge them to defend their original stance if they still believe in it.",
        "progression_name": "AI Feedback Test"
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "7c896e45-c53d-4633-8dbf-f7a279616960",
        "lesson_activity.key": "dec38672-8746-478d-ab54-81511599fc40"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "79b25bd5-b338-40e3-b056-f73c714880ef",
      "position": 9,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-comments\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Discuss:** *What type of suggestions were more useful than others?*\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-lightbulb-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Discussion Goal:** The goal is for students to see that useful feedback isn't just a bot agreeing with them, but rather the specific, logical pushback that helps them find gaps in their evidence. Students should identify that the best suggestions are those that challenge them to move away from vague \"be careful\" rules and toward clear guidance based on their own experiences."
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "79b25bd5-b338-40e3-b056-f73c714880ef",
        "lesson_activity.key": "dec38672-8746-478d-ab54-81511599fc40"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "0513719b-af2d-4e81-87de-797ccb346480",
      "position": 10,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa-solid fa-bullseye-arrow\"></i> **Goal of this activity:** Students apply feedback received to their Generate and Judge project and add any additional guidance and tips that they want to highlight.",
        "duration": "10",
        "name": "Project Iteration"
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "0513719b-af2d-4e81-87de-797ccb346480",
        "lesson_activity.key": "dec38672-8746-478d-ab54-81511599fc40"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "de8294ca-1094-4283-a0ff-22b8e78a43e8",
      "position": 11,
      "properties": {
        "description": "Use the discussions you had during the warm up to add additional guidance to your Generate and Judge Project. Then use the feedback from the AI Reviewers to make improvements.\n",
        "remarks": true
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "de8294ca-1094-4283-a0ff-22b8e78a43e8",
        "lesson_activity.key": "dec38672-8746-478d-ab54-81511599fc40"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "e135fb32-4476-4445-8ce9-819927ca3c02",
      "position": 12,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-desktop\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Transition:** Direct students to Lesson 6, Level 4. Students implement the feedback they received to their project to make improvements.\n",
        "progression_name": "Project Iteration",
        "tips": [
          {
            "type": "teachingTip",
            "markdown": "Push students beyond vague language like \"check it\" or \"don't trust everything.\" Ask:\n- What specifically should someone look for?\n- What detail made you lower your trust during testing?\n- What pattern kept showing up?\n- Encourage conditional thinking instead of absolute rules."
          }
        ]
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "e135fb32-4476-4445-8ce9-819927ca3c02",
        "lesson_activity.key": "dec38672-8746-478d-ab54-81511599fc40"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "eaae5a92-3eb0-430b-865c-13b43ae6c48e",
      "position": 13,
      "properties": {
        "description": "above is new"
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "eaae5a92-3eb0-430b-865c-13b43ae6c48e",
        "lesson_activity.key": "dec38672-8746-478d-ab54-81511599fc40"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "56feea60-c504-47c0-a4db-09aa1c6cae7b",
      "position": 1,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Review the lesson objectives.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Review the Question of the Day.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-comments\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Discuss:** Click through the animated slide to display the prompts.\n- *Would you put \"getting feedback on your work\" in the Use AI, Don't Use AI, or It Depends pile?*\n- *What makes it hard to sort?*\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-lightbulb-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Discussion Goal:** The most important condition students should name is whether the feedback-giver represents the actual audience. AI can check logic, clarity, and completeness, but AI doesn't know who your specific reader is. A strong response sounds like: \"It depends on whether the AI actually understands who I'm writing for — a younger student needs different feedback than a teacher.\" If students say \"AI can be wrong,\" push further: \"Wrong about what, specifically? What can't AI assess that your actual reader could?\" Students who reach the idea that AI lacks the lived experience of the intended audience are showing the deepest understanding of the day's lesson."
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "56feea60-c504-47c0-a4db-09aa1c6cae7b",
        "lesson_activity.key": "b935594c-6d1b-4b2e-a1b8-4629d26245bb"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "17a48065-19c4-4a46-80ac-67b51000c132",
      "position": 1,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa-solid fa-bullseye-arrow\"></i> **Goal of this activity:** Students connect their own experience of being misled to how AI can produce false information that sounds completely convincing — building the instinct to verify before trusting, not after.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Read the short explanation of this true story.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-comments\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Discuss:** Click through the animated slide to display the prompts.\n- *Have you ever believed something that turned out to be wrong?*\n- *What made it seem true at the time?*\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-lightbulb-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Discussion Goal:** Listen for students who can name a specific reason something felt true (confidence, repetition, or a trusted source) those are exactly the conditions that make AI misinformation hard to catch.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Introduce the roles of AI fact-checkers and investigative journalists."
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "17a48065-19c4-4a46-80ac-67b51000c132",
        "lesson_activity.key": "1eda96bf-6153-42fc-8db4-009cde952d2b"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "b358988a-840a-4760-9ec0-2f257faacca7",
      "position": 2,
      "properties": {
        "description": "The lawyers didn't do what a journalist would have done — independently verify each specific claim before relying on it. That verification habit is a professional skill, and people build careers around it.\n",
        "remarks": true
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "b358988a-840a-4760-9ec0-2f257faacca7",
        "lesson_activity.key": "1eda96bf-6153-42fc-8db4-009cde952d2b"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "4644d252-f867-411e-9168-1aafca60e480",
      "position": 3,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Introduce the lesson objectives.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Introduce the Question of the Day."
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "4644d252-f867-411e-9168-1aafca60e480",
        "lesson_activity.key": "1eda96bf-6153-42fc-8db4-009cde952d2b"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "70bd613a-d4b5-4c49-b1a8-8381b9412325",
      "position": 1,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa-solid fa-bullseye-arrow\"></i> **Goal of this activity:** Students visualize how AI learns from patterns in training data and why that process can produce biased or incomplete results even without any intention to mislead.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Place students in groups of three or four students.\n\u000b<i class=\"fa fa-file-text-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Distribute:** Give each student an index card or a half sheet of paper for a quick draw activity.\n",
        "duration": "10",
        "name": "What's an Apple?"
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "70bd613a-d4b5-4c49-b1a8-8381b9412325",
        "lesson_activity.key": "6491e8f5-578e-4f42-88b3-6bef7e433665"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "4832d614-d2bc-4323-b0ae-245f1ca6276b",
      "position": 2,
      "properties": {
        "description": "AI generates new content based on the patterns it sees over and over again in its training data. Sometimes those patterns don’t fully represent the whole truth.\n",
        "remarks": true
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "4832d614-d2bc-4323-b0ae-245f1ca6276b",
        "lesson_activity.key": "6491e8f5-578e-4f42-88b3-6bef7e433665"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "77b0fbfd-2ef0-495c-b40a-4e881f834ae5",
      "position": 3,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Give students 30 seconds to draw an apple. Students should share their drawings with the group and identify common patterns in their drawings (stem, leaf, red color, indentation, etc.).\n"
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "77b0fbfd-2ef0-495c-b40a-4e881f834ae5",
        "lesson_activity.key": "6491e8f5-578e-4f42-88b3-6bef7e433665"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "3a89d9ea-6784-4f34-a366-d9dfd5c96240",
      "position": 4,
      "properties": {
        "description": "Look at all of these together. If an AI learned what an apple is only from these drawings, what would it think an apple looks like?\n",
        "remarks": true
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "3a89d9ea-6784-4f34-a366-d9dfd5c96240",
        "lesson_activity.key": "6491e8f5-578e-4f42-88b3-6bef7e433665"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "b34c9075-d361-4714-b8e2-ed0475edf9a7",
      "position": 5,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-comments\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Discuss:** Click through the animated slide to display the prompts.\n- *Is this an apple?*\n- *Would an AI know that?*\n- *What kinds of apples did your training data miss?*\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-lightbulb-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Discussion Goal:** Listen for students who notice that their drawings all defaulted to the same apple — probably red, whole, with a stem — and can name what that version left out (green apples, sliced apples, apples with bruises, varieties they eat at home). The strongest responses will connect the gap not just to what was missing but to why it was missing: everyone drew from the same mental image, which means the \"training data\" was narrow before anyone even picked up a pencil. That's the move that makes the apple activity land as more than a drawing exercise — it becomes an explanation for why AI outputs can be incomplete even when no one intended them to be.",
        "tips": [
          {
            "type": "teachingTip",
            "markdown": "Resist the urge to explain bias before students notice it themselves. Let the pattern recognition happen first, then name it. When students see that their \"training data\" missed a real apple, the concept lands on its own. Push students to connect this to whose drawings were included and whose were left out.\n"
          }
        ]
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "b34c9075-d361-4714-b8e2-ed0475edf9a7",
        "lesson_activity.key": "6491e8f5-578e-4f42-88b3-6bef7e433665"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "abe04512-72b9-4d1b-ad2d-51993eae3ef7",
      "position": 6,
      "properties": {
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "abe04512-72b9-4d1b-ad2d-51993eae3ef7",
        "lesson_activity.key": "6491e8f5-578e-4f42-88b3-6bef7e433665"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "4a387cb8-1344-4fb5-b08e-9d711b717e76",
      "position": 7,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa-solid fa-bullseye-arrow\"></i> **Goal of this activity:** Students explore how AI tends to sound overconfident and make guesses, then learn strategies to verify AI outputs and write a tip in their guide to AI for their chosen audience.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Recall that AI generates based on what it learns from patterns in its training data. Explain that it sounds confident, but that doesn't mean it's always right or complete.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Click through the animated slide to explain there are steps we can take to verify information and text AI provides but it's always a good idea to bring in a human to double check.",
        "duration": "25",
        "name": "Verifying AI"
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "4a387cb8-1344-4fb5-b08e-9d711b717e76",
        "lesson_activity.key": "6491e8f5-578e-4f42-88b3-6bef7e433665"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "03c6e04f-f932-4690-9196-071e060e8453",
      "position": 8,
      "properties": {
        "description": "Instead of asking \"can I trust this?\", we break it down: Where did this come from? Do other sources agree? Is this recent? If it affects a real decision, has a human checked it?\n",
        "remarks": true
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "03c6e04f-f932-4690-9196-071e060e8453",
        "lesson_activity.key": "6491e8f5-578e-4f42-88b3-6bef7e433665"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "80fe4f0f-0d4c-40f6-a51e-f0914e891eca",
      "position": 9,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-comments\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Discuss:** *Which of these tips would have helped the lawyers from the story earlier?*\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-lightbulb-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Discussion Goal:** Students should apply specific checklist items to the lawyer story — not just \"they should have checked it\" but naming which step would have caught the error and what that would have looked like in practice. A strong response sounds like: \"If they had asked AI for its sources, it would have had to admit it couldn't cite them\" or \"A trusted legal database would have shown none of those cases existed.\" If students stay vague, ask: \"Which step on the list? What exactly would that step have looked like for a lawyer working on a real case?\" Push until they name a specific action and connect it to a specific point in the story."
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "80fe4f0f-0d4c-40f6-a51e-f0914e891eca",
        "lesson_activity.key": "6491e8f5-578e-4f42-88b3-6bef7e433665"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "74a59ff6-6d38-4dab-8dcd-7ffecab3ce2d",
      "position": 10,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-desktop\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Transition:** Direct students to Lesson 7, Level 1 to complete Levels 1 through 3.\n- Level 1: Students learn more about AI's overconfidence.\n- Level 2: Students read about strategies for verifying AI output.\n- Level 3: Students add tips and advice to their project for verifying AI output.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-refresh\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Circulate:** Look for students who are drawing directly on the lawyer story or the apple experiment to support their tip. If a student is stuck, ask: \"What is one thing you knew after today that you did not know before? Write that down for your reader.\"",
        "tips": [
          {
            "type": "teachingTip",
            "markdown": "Push students away from vague warnings like \"AI can be wrong\" and toward specific, actionable guidance, the kind a real person could actually follow. If a student writes \"always fact check AI,\" ask them: fact check it how? Using what? That one follow-up question usually unlocks a much stronger tip.\n"
          }
        ]
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "74a59ff6-6d38-4dab-8dcd-7ffecab3ce2d",
        "lesson_activity.key": "6491e8f5-578e-4f42-88b3-6bef7e433665"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "f59ce695-297b-4f78-9239-af7b79a365d6",
      "position": 11,
      "properties": {
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "f59ce695-297b-4f78-9239-af7b79a365d6",
        "lesson_activity.key": "6491e8f5-578e-4f42-88b3-6bef7e433665"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "4945d7db-75b4-4c45-8a76-4023c5e6288e",
      "position": 1,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Review the lesson objectives.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Review the Question of the Day.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-comments\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Discuss:** *After today, what would you tell a friend who thinks AI is always right?*\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-lightbulb-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Discussion Goal:** Students should explain the mechanism, not just the outcome. A strong response sounds like: \"AI predicts what sounds right based on patterns — so it produces confident text even when the thing it's describing doesn't exist. It's not trying to lie, it just can't tell the difference between something true and something that fits the pattern.\" If students say \"AI can make mistakes\" without explaining why, ask: \"But why does it sound so sure? Why doesn't it warn you when it's guessing?\" That question usually unlocks the explanation. Students who can describe the mechanism — pattern prediction without truth-checking — have reached the core concept of the lesson."
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "4945d7db-75b4-4c45-8a76-4023c5e6288e",
        "lesson_activity.key": "511708df-80a5-4f6d-b95a-aca8d28faaa1"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "6105b233-ad36-4219-8373-8657d4ddcfa9",
      "position": 1,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa-solid fa-bullseye-arrow\"></i> **Goal of this activity:** Students explore how small pieces of public data can be combined to reveal sensitive information through a high-stakes scenario.\n"
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "6105b233-ad36-4219-8373-8657d4ddcfa9",
        "lesson_activity.key": "cc109b38-4223-45e4-b0dd-441ca7fa4624"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "cd6a592b-bdf1-4ed5-87e8-f74b9e32a2ce",
      "position": 2,
      "properties": {
        "description": "Imagine your favorite streamer suddenly stops broadcasting because someone showed up at their house. No one knew where they lived, but they posted one photo. How could that one photo lead someone straight to their door? Today we're starting with a mystery. A famous streamer named Z-Tech went dark because someone found their house using nothing but a selfie. We're going to see if we can figure out how that happened.\n",
        "remarks": true
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "cd6a592b-bdf1-4ed5-87e8-f74b9e32a2ce",
        "lesson_activity.key": "cc109b38-4223-45e4-b0dd-441ca7fa4624"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "33ae7478-f225-4ce8-a61f-619e12d0f3a2",
      "position": 3,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** With a partner, students examine the selfie to find three specific details in the background that could be used to pinpoint Z-Tech's location.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-refresh\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Circulate:** Look for students who are looking past the person in the photo and at the background. Ask: \"What does that bus number tell you about the school district?\" or \"How many stores in this city carry that specific soda flavor?\"",
        "tips": [
          {
            "type": "teachingTip",
            "markdown": "Consider zooming in on a few different areas of the sample selfie image so that students can see more detail.\n"
          }
        ]
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "33ae7478-f225-4ce8-a61f-619e12d0f3a2",
        "lesson_activity.key": "cc109b38-4223-45e4-b0dd-441ca7fa4624"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "5fa35899-46c4-4b80-857c-a1a1f9a11b06",
      "position": 4,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-comments\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Discuss:** *What could you determine from what you saw in the image?*\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-lightbulb-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Discussion Goal:** Students should trace specific inference chains — following one detail to the next until it reveals something sensitive. A strong response sounds like: \"The bus number tells you the route, the route tells you the neighborhood, and with the school name visible you could narrow the address down to a few blocks.\" If students stay general (\"there's a lot of information in photos\"), ask: \"Give me one specific piece of data from that image. What can you infer from just that one thing? Now what does that combine with?\" The concept to reach is that no single piece of data is necessarily sensitive — it's the combination that creates risk. Students who can demonstrate one full inference chain have the key idea.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Introduce the lesson objectives.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Introduce the Question of the Day."
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "5fa35899-46c4-4b80-857c-a1a1f9a11b06",
        "lesson_activity.key": "cc109b38-4223-45e4-b0dd-441ca7fa4624"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "ccecc185-ec35-47e6-9613-110a5ec87a78",
      "position": 1,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa-solid fa-bullseye-arrow\"></i> **Goal of this activity:** Students will learn how to classify different types of data and will explore how oversharing private and sensitive data has hidden risks.\n",
        "duration": "25",
        "name": "Privacy and Safety Exploration"
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "ccecc185-ec35-47e6-9613-110a5ec87a78",
        "lesson_activity.key": "d68f3932-1b69-4d73-80c4-078703c1e7c5"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "e87f1289-bff6-4c8e-90b9-f289cefa85b5",
      "position": 2,
      "properties": {
        "description": "Now that we've seen how a single photo can reveal a location, let's look at the different types of data we generate every day. Data can usually be classified into three different categories: public, private, and sensitive.\n",
        "remarks": true
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "e87f1289-bff6-4c8e-90b9-f289cefa85b5",
        "lesson_activity.key": "d68f3932-1b69-4d73-80c4-078703c1e7c5"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "87603214-695a-4e62-bae3-4dbf054af0af",
      "position": 3,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Click through the animated slide to introduce the types of data and examples in the image.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Define public data.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Define private data.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Define sensitive data.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-file-text-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Distribute:** Give each student a copy of the Privacy and Safety Exploration activity guide."
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "87603214-695a-4e62-bae3-4dbf054af0af",
        "lesson_activity.key": "d68f3932-1b69-4d73-80c4-078703c1e7c5"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "fb6ef0d6-ff5a-43e8-9547-f34e8765d389",
      "position": 4,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-desktop\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Transition:** Direct students to Lesson 8, Level 1 to complete Levels 1 through 2.\n- Level 1: Students choose one or more of the digital artifacts and document public, private, and sensitive information in their activity guide.\n- Level 2: Students give the same digital artifact to an AI chatbot to see what it might determine about the individual based on the information in the artifact.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-refresh\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Circulate:** Challenge students to come up with as many examples of data as possible and to document them in their activity guide. When interacting with the AI chatbot, encourage students to try different combinations of data to see how the results might vary.",
        "progression_name": "AI Testing"
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "fb6ef0d6-ff5a-43e8-9547-f34e8765d389",
        "lesson_activity.key": "d68f3932-1b69-4d73-80c4-078703c1e7c5"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "f48b4f46-4e4e-46fa-a75d-986a86721f6c",
      "position": 5,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Have students complete the Safety and Security Debrief section in their activity guide.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-comments\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Discuss:** *What patterns did you recognize that separate public, private, and sensitive data?*\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-lightbulb-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Discussion Goal:** Students can quickly share some ways that they classified data and how they chose to differentiate. Some sample patterns that they might identify include:\n- Public data: General preferences, fandoms, or regional pride that help you connect with others but don't put your safety at risk.  (gaming handle, social media likes, t-shirt style)\n- Private data: Information that is unique to you but doesn't necessarily reveal your location. It’s often used for security questions or official records (legal name, birth year, allergies)\n- Sensitive data: Data that reveals exactly where you are, where you live, or your daily routine (house number, wi-fi name)\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Have students suggest how they would change the Sensitive Data example, then click through the animated slide to show an example.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Students should complete the Anonymize the Data section in their activity guide."
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "f48b4f46-4e4e-46fa-a75d-986a86721f6c",
        "lesson_activity.key": "d68f3932-1b69-4d73-80c4-078703c1e7c5"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "c991f9e5-f095-4ae5-b4b3-1cbb1e49d926",
      "position": 6,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa-solid fa-bullseye-arrow\"></i> **Goal of this activity:** Students will explore an interactive panel level on either deepfake technology or hidden metadata to learn more about safety risks that are becoming more common with AI.\n",
        "duration": "10",
        "name": "Privacy and Safety Mini-Lessons"
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "c991f9e5-f095-4ae5-b4b3-1cbb1e49d926",
        "lesson_activity.key": "d68f3932-1b69-4d73-80c4-078703c1e7c5"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "575c26d5-b6ae-4ebd-b994-2b4181360b5a",
      "position": 7,
      "properties": {
        "description": "AI can be a powerful tool for creativity, but it also comes with risks if we don't understand how it works. As we look at these safety spotlights, we’re going to practice thinking critically so we can make intentional choices about when and how to use these systems safely\n",
        "remarks": true
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "575c26d5-b6ae-4ebd-b994-2b4181360b5a",
        "lesson_activity.key": "d68f3932-1b69-4d73-80c4-078703c1e7c5"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "026581b1-e926-4e9a-8544-f8144e21cd9b",
      "position": 8,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-desktop\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Transition:** Direct students to Lesson 8, Level 3. Students select between a mini-lesson to explore a topic of their choice.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-refresh\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Circulate:** Ask students what surprised them.",
        "progression_name": "AI Safety and Privacy Mini-Lesson"
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "026581b1-e926-4e9a-8544-f8144e21cd9b",
        "lesson_activity.key": "d68f3932-1b69-4d73-80c4-078703c1e7c5"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "67ed66c4-9ca7-400a-a606-357f4eeeba3f",
      "position": 9,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Use the blue play icon to start the Give One, Get One activity. Prompt students to find a partner and share something they learned from the AI Safety and Privacy mini-lesson. After both students share, they should find a new partner and repeat the process.\n"
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "67ed66c4-9ca7-400a-a606-357f4eeeba3f",
        "lesson_activity.key": "d68f3932-1b69-4d73-80c4-078703c1e7c5"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "387a6a8e-b89e-4deb-9554-8d392303c558",
      "position": 1,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Review the lesson objectives.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Review the Question of the Day.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-comments\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Discuss:** *Have you accidentally included any private or sensitive information in AI chats before?*\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-lightbulb-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Discussion Goal:** Students should name a specific habit and connect it to a specific risk they now understand — not \"I'll be more careful\" but something like \"I've typed my location into a chatbot when I was asking about things near me, and now I realize that combined with other things I've shared could reveal a lot.\" The follow-up push: \"What specifically would you stop including, and what could that combine with to create a risk?\" Pull students from general commitments toward specific, concrete behavioral changes grounded in the inference chain concept from the warm-up.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Review the Key Vocabulary."
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "387a6a8e-b89e-4deb-9554-8d392303c558",
        "lesson_activity.key": "be9a1cab-aad1-4c02-b1c6-61041caf8377"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "d4a4b28f-a834-4226-82c8-16203d856616",
      "position": 1,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-video-camera\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Video:** Play the video.\n\n**Questions to consider with the video:** \n- What is Jordan's big tip or guidance for using AI? (hint: It's at minute 2:45-3:10)",
        "tips": [
          {
            "type": "teachingTip",
            "markdown": "Videos are used throughout the curriculum to spark discussions, supplement key concepts with additional explanations and examples, and expose students to the various roles and backgrounds of individuals in computer science. While interacting with the video, turn on closed captioning so students can also read along as they watch. To encourage active engagement and reflection, use one or more of the strategies discussed in the [Guide to Curriculum Videos](https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Y-kGl_pc2afuSBKhKkdulu53X50mc7T-RQZA4vGLpY4/edit?usp=sharing).\n"
          }
        ]
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "d4a4b28f-a834-4226-82c8-16203d856616",
        "lesson_activity.key": "0cad6689-5fda-435a-bcbf-d24ab01ba6c0"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "65db6f66-bfc5-47fe-9dd3-e3806588a6be",
      "position": 2,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-comments\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Discuss:** *When does AI make your work better, and when does it just make it easier?*\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-lightbulb-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Discussion Goal:** Listen for students drawing the same distinction Jordan did — that AI becomes a problem when it replaces human energy and judgment, but becomes powerful when it amplifies what a person already brings to their work.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Introduce the lesson objectives.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Introduce the Question of the Day.\n"
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "65db6f66-bfc5-47fe-9dd3-e3806588a6be",
        "lesson_activity.key": "0cad6689-5fda-435a-bcbf-d24ab01ba6c0"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "3a6030c8-f857-4a4d-afc6-92bff3ebc2b2",
      "position": 1,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa-solid fa-bullseye-arrow\"></i> **Goal of this activity:** Students should experience AI feedback as a tool for strengthening their own thinking.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-desktop\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Transition:** Direct students to Lesson 9, Level 1 to complete Levels 1 through 3.\n- Level 1: Students save their project to their Backpack.\n- Level 2: Students use the Rubric Reviewer Bot to get feedback on their project.\n- Level 3: Students create a custom chatbot to get feedback on their project.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-refresh\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Circulate:** Ask students \"what is one thing the bot flagged that you actually agree with?\" This separates students who are thinking critically about the feedback from those who are accepting or rejecting it without engaging. As students work on Level 3, connect this back to the Generate and Judge Project — what purpose is this chatbot serving and how does it connect to the goal and audience that the student identified?\n",
        "duration": "15",
        "name": "Rubric Reviewer",
        "progression_name": "Rubric Reviewer"
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "3a6030c8-f857-4a4d-afc6-92bff3ebc2b2",
        "lesson_activity.key": "84dd22a6-2f8d-4293-96b4-821072a631de"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "a392c0f7-3635-4ecd-8dab-d2be676649d9",
      "position": 2,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-comments\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Discuss:** *What is the most important thing you have learned about using AI responsibly?*\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-lightbulb-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Discussion Goal:** A strong response names a specific experience from the unit and connects it to a general principle — something like: \"When I tested the image generator and it gave me the same 'healthy meal' every time no matter how I phrased it, I realized AI treats one perspective as the default — so I have to be explicit about what I actually want.\" A weak response sounds like: \"AI can be helpful but you have to be careful.\" The difference is specificity: does the student have a real unit experience that grounds their claim? If not, ask them to look at their Field Notes and find the moment that surprised them most — that moment is usually where their real position is. Students who can trace their claim to a specific test result are ready to write a strong final statement.\n"
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "a392c0f7-3635-4ecd-8dab-d2be676649d9",
        "lesson_activity.key": "84dd22a6-2f8d-4293-96b4-821072a631de"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "eed84a8d-03b9-42a7-8b2e-6576fdbcef6d",
      "position": 3,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa-solid fa-bullseye-arrow\"></i> **Goal of this activity:** Students synthesize their learning into a single evidence-backed statement that anchors their guide with a clear personal position on responsible AI use.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Recall the project and connection to the role of an auditor.",
        "duration": "15",
        "name": "Finalizing the Project",
        "tips": [
          {
            "type": "teachingTip",
            "markdown": "This is the moment where the AI Auditor career frame pays off. Students have been documenting like auditors since Lesson 3. Now their guide should read like an audit report — not \"here are some tips\" but \"here is what I found and here is what it means.\" When circulating during Level 4, push back on vague final statements by asking: \"Which field notes finding is this based on? Can you point to it?\" Students who can point to their documentation have earned their conclusion.\n"
          }
        ]
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "eed84a8d-03b9-42a7-8b2e-6576fdbcef6d",
        "lesson_activity.key": "84dd22a6-2f8d-4293-96b4-821072a631de"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "44b195d8-d418-4370-97fc-66334b911063",
      "position": 4,
      "properties": {
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "44b195d8-d418-4370-97fc-66334b911063",
        "lesson_activity.key": "84dd22a6-2f8d-4293-96b4-821072a631de"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "b711f426-fbe0-4d13-bd43-0d483d91ac4d",
      "position": 5,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Explain to students that they will finalize their project and should take these steps as they do so.\n"
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "b711f426-fbe0-4d13-bd43-0d483d91ac4d",
        "lesson_activity.key": "84dd22a6-2f8d-4293-96b4-821072a631de"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "2cf080ac-313e-4889-98a0-6832ab3d4b59",
      "position": 6,
      "properties": {
        "description": "This is not a rule you found online. It is something you actually believe based on what you discovered and tested in this unit. Your reader should feel like it came from a real person who thought hard about it.\n",
        "remarks": true
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "2cf080ac-313e-4889-98a0-6832ab3d4b59",
        "lesson_activity.key": "84dd22a6-2f8d-4293-96b4-821072a631de"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "09457530-44de-4531-8b14-4a191cf50c70",
      "position": 7,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-desktop\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Transition:** Direct students to Lesson 9, Level 4. Students finish their Generate and Judge Projects.\n<i class=\"fa fa-refresh\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Circulate:** Push back on vague statements. If a student writes \"AI can help as long as you are careful,\" ask: \"Careful about what specifically?\"",
        "progression_name": "Finalize Your Project",
        "tips": [
          {
            "type": "teachingTip",
            "markdown": "If students are stuck, ask them to look back at their evidence and find the moment that surprised them most. That moment is usually where their best statement is hiding.\n"
          }
        ]
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "09457530-44de-4531-8b14-4a191cf50c70",
        "lesson_activity.key": "84dd22a6-2f8d-4293-96b4-821072a631de"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "945f9cf0-5cff-40c1-8231-c8455692182c",
      "position": 8,
      "properties": {
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "945f9cf0-5cff-40c1-8231-c8455692182c",
        "lesson_activity.key": "84dd22a6-2f8d-4293-96b4-821072a631de"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "bfe01452-c737-44ed-b366-0923dc3a76a5",
      "position": 1,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Review the lesson objectives.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Review the Question of the Day.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-comments\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Discuss:** *Looking at your finished guide, what is your favorite or most important tip or guidance you wrote? What experience from this unit showed you how important it is?*\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-lightbulb-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Discussion Goal:** Students will connect at least one piece of guidance in their finished guide to a specific experience or discovery from the unit, demonstrating that their advice is grounded in evidence rather than assumption."
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "bfe01452-c737-44ed-b366-0923dc3a76a5",
        "lesson_activity.key": "6b29878b-22d7-4932-80f3-f3f33fcf2710"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "d0dd8413-4657-4f85-b507-e2a84e6b0c0f",
      "position": 1,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa-solid fa-bullseye-arrow\"></i> **Goal of this activity:** Students apply the potential of AI they explored in the warm-up to a structured debate about the human's role in getting the most out of it.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Have students think silently about how much AI can do.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Ask students to share their predictions about what AI might be able to do in the future.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-comments\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Discuss:** *AI can do extraordinary things. What role should humans play to make the most of that potential?*\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-lightbulb-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Discussion Goal:** Students should connect AI's growing potential to the value of human involvement. Listen for language that frames humans as unlocking that potential.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Introduce the lesson objectives.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Introduce the Question of the Day."
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "d0dd8413-4657-4f85-b507-e2a84e6b0c0f",
        "lesson_activity.key": "ee699646-156e-4a25-85be-1869aea0720f"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "041ddf38-01ce-4cb6-b156-4bff236e1ede",
      "position": 2,
      "properties": {
        "description": "Today, you are defending a position about how humans should interact with AI.\n",
        "remarks": true
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "041ddf38-01ce-4cb6-b156-4bff236e1ede",
        "lesson_activity.key": "ee699646-156e-4a25-85be-1869aea0720f"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "14fb0cd9-ebf8-424c-b28c-12a2d4f5480f",
      "position": 1,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-file-text-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Distribute:** Give each student a copy of The Final Verdict activity guide.\n"
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "14fb0cd9-ebf8-424c-b28c-12a2d4f5480f",
        "lesson_activity.key": "9f4816a8-2fb5-458b-a52f-03982c3708c3"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "8bf16170-73c0-4cc5-b982-09226649ab3d",
      "position": 2,
      "properties": {
        "description": "Today you'll take part in a mini mock trial where you defend a position about how humans should interact with AI. Use your activity guide to focus on clear claims and specific evidence from our unit.\n",
        "remarks": true
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "8bf16170-73c0-4cc5-b982-09226649ab3d",
        "lesson_activity.key": "9f4816a8-2fb5-458b-a52f-03982c3708c3"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "18df3cc0-a654-40d8-9b0a-2477908c4f5c",
      "position": 3,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Introduce the mock trial and that they will argue one of the sides using evidence from this unit. They'll work with a team to prepare their case. Explain each position and give a short classroom example (e.g., using AI to draft a quick email vs. editing AI-drafted email for accuracy and tone). Then divide the class into three groups and assign each group a position (Passenger, Pilot, and Jury).\n",
        "tips": [
          {
            "type": "teachingTip",
            "markdown": "Assign roles so each student practices both proposing and critiquing evidence across rounds.\n"
          }
        ]
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "18df3cc0-a654-40d8-9b0a-2477908c4f5c",
        "lesson_activity.key": "9f4816a8-2fb5-458b-a52f-03982c3708c3"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "1058969a-53e5-4a7b-a1a0-928a4e121438",
      "position": 4,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Explain the Pilot and Passenger example using AI to draft an email vs. writing and sending an AI-drafted email.\n"
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "1058969a-53e5-4a7b-a1a0-928a4e121438",
        "lesson_activity.key": "9f4816a8-2fb5-458b-a52f-03982c3708c3"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "d4bd825f-92b9-4dce-823a-1b8c5987bf48",
      "position": 5,
      "properties": {
        "description": "Pilot and Passenger describe how involved the human chooses to be. AI is the engine and it powers the work, but it doesn't have opinions or make choices. Neither position is wrong — both have real strengths. Your job today is to defend a position about how humans should interact with AI. Focus on clear claims and specific evidence from our unit.\n",
        "remarks": true
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "d4bd825f-92b9-4dce-823a-1b8c5987bf48",
        "lesson_activity.key": "9f4816a8-2fb5-458b-a52f-03982c3708c3"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "73179fdf-6754-4faa-97cf-f357330f8513",
      "position": 6,
      "properties": {
        "description": "Today you'll take part in a mini mock trial where you defend a position about how humans should interact with AI. Focus on clear claims and specific evidence from our unit.\n",
        "remarks": true
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "73179fdf-6754-4faa-97cf-f357330f8513",
        "lesson_activity.key": "9f4816a8-2fb5-458b-a52f-03982c3708c3"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "ea735f77-e71d-4905-a720-31a02aa03bf4",
      "position": 7,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Introduce the Passenger position.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Introduce the Pilot position.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Introduce the Jury position."
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "ea735f77-e71d-4905-a720-31a02aa03bf4",
        "lesson_activity.key": "9f4816a8-2fb5-458b-a52f-03982c3708c3"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "74350671-0965-4242-be7a-c4cacd42fd55",
      "position": 8,
      "properties": {
        "description": "The trial follows a short script: each side gives an opening statement, presents evidence with a short cross-exam, and then the jury deliberates and decides.\n",
        "remarks": true
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "74350671-0965-4242-be7a-c4cacd42fd55",
        "lesson_activity.key": "9f4816a8-2fb5-458b-a52f-03982c3708c3"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "f74225b7-b43e-4aef-9e3e-a0bbdd489838",
      "position": 9,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Walk students through each stage and set timing expectations (for example: 1 minute opening, 1 minute per evidence, 1 minute cross-exam, 5 minute jury).\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Have students participate in the mock trial by starting with their opening statements, then do cross-examination, and conclude with a final verdict.",
        "tips": [
          {
            "type": "teachingTip",
            "markdown": "Keep the trial tightly scoped and time-box each phase (opening, evidence, cross-exam, deliberation) so the activity stays quick and focused.  If class size is large, run paired mini-trials or act as one side so everyone practices roles.\n"
          }
        ]
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "f74225b7-b43e-4aef-9e3e-a0bbdd489838",
        "lesson_activity.key": "9f4816a8-2fb5-458b-a52f-03982c3708c3"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "a36ff224-6c42-476b-a125-bdcba3d80e60",
      "position": 10,
      "properties": {
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "a36ff224-6c42-476b-a125-bdcba3d80e60",
        "lesson_activity.key": "9f4816a8-2fb5-458b-a52f-03982c3708c3"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "608bdc63-f29c-42ff-9fe3-176bb10dd56e",
      "position": 11,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Summarize the class verdict and highlight examples that show why human judgment matters (bias, hallucination, data inference, credibility checks).\n",
        "tips": [
          {
            "type": "teachingTip",
            "markdown": "Reinforce nuance: acknowledge benefits of AI for speed and scale while stressing when oversight is needed. Invite students to suggest one classroom guideline for using AI responsibly going forward.\n"
          }
        ]
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "608bdc63-f29c-42ff-9fe3-176bb10dd56e",
        "lesson_activity.key": "9f4816a8-2fb5-458b-a52f-03982c3708c3"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "d984248c-0b4b-4d16-863f-21be20393045",
      "position": 12,
      "properties": {
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "d984248c-0b4b-4d16-863f-21be20393045",
        "lesson_activity.key": "9f4816a8-2fb5-458b-a52f-03982c3708c3"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "d1820aaa-72eb-4bc6-b248-334beb1e3716",
      "position": 1,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Review the lesson objectives.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Review the Question of the Day.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-comments\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Discuss:** Click through the animated slide to display the prompts.\n- *How did your thinking about AI's capabilities, limitations, or risks change during this unit?*\n- *What uncertainties or questions do you still have about when humans should rely on AI?*\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-lightbulb-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Discussion Goal:** Surface how students' views shifted from simple judgments (AI is good/bad) to more nuanced positions that weigh benefits and risks. Listen for responses that reference specific investigations (bias, hallucinations, data privacy, co-creation). If discussion stalls, prompt: \"Which investigation surprised you most, and why?\" or \"What would make you trust an AI recommendation more?\"",
        "tips": [
          {
            "type": "teachingTip",
            "markdown": "Encourage students to respond to each other briefly (one follow-up question or connection). If time is tight, limit to two students per prompt and collect quick takeaways on the board.\n"
          }
        ]
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "d1820aaa-72eb-4bc6-b248-334beb1e3716",
        "lesson_activity.key": "549fdff2-91bf-441f-a5f0-204f08749bad"
      }
    },
